        "url": "/whitepapers/it-leaders-guide-to-linux-device-management-fr",
        "title": "It leaders guide to linux device management fr",
        "lastModifiedAt": 1778183827000,
        "htmlId": "articles--it-leaders-guide-to---382ccb3bd3",
        "sectionRelativeRepoPath": "IT-leaders-guide-to-Linux-device-management-fr.md",
        "meta": {
          "articleTitle": "Le guide du responsable IT pour la gestion des appareils Linux",
          "authorFullName": "n/a",
          "authorGitHubUsername": "fleet-release",
          "category": "whitepaper",
          "publishedOn": "2026-04-20",
          "description": "Comblez le fossé de la gestion Linux. Guide pour responsables IT : analyse de rentabilité, sécurité, conformité et choix de la solution.",
          "articleImageUrl": "/images/articles/IT-leaders-guide-to-Linux-device-management-cover-image-504x336@2x.png",
          "whitepaperFilename": "IT-leaders-guide-to-Linux-device-management-fr.pdf",
          "formHeadline": "Combler le fossé de la gestion Linux avec Fleet",
          "introductionTextBlockOne": "Linux dépasse désormais 5 % de part de marché sur le poste de travail. L’enquête Stack Overflow publiée en 2025 auprès des développeurs montre que près de 30 % d’entre eux utilisent Linux comme système d’exploitation principal au travail.",
          "introductionTextBlockTwo": "Les contributeurs les plus importants — développeurs, ingénieurs et professionnels de la sécurité — choisissent Linux. Dans la plupart des organisations, ces appareils sont gérés par des scripts maison et des outils de gestion de configuration comme Ansible, Puppet ou Chef. Ces approches fonctionnent, mais elles ne remplacent pas une plateforme de gestion dédiée pour la conformité, la visibilité et les audits."
        }
      },
      {
        "url": "/whitepapers/it-leaders-guide-to-linux-device-management",
        "title": "It leaders guide to linux device management",
        "lastModifiedAt": 1778183827000,
        "htmlId": "articles--it-leaders-guide-to---e08e80d17d",
        "sectionRelativeRepoPath": "IT-leaders-guide-to-Linux-device-management.md",
        "meta": {
          "articleTitle": "The IT leader's guide to Linux device management",
          "authorFullName": "n/a",
          "authorGitHubUsername": "fleet-release",
          "category": "whitepaper",
          "publishedOn": "2026-04-20",
          "description": "Close the Linux management gap. A guide to help IT leaders understand the business case, security, compliance, and choosing the right solution.",
          "articleImageUrl": "/images/articles/IT-leaders-guide-to-Linux-device-management-cover-image-504x336@2x.png",
          "whitepaperFilename": "IT-leaders-guide-to-Linux-device-management.pdf",
          "formHeadline": "Learn how to close the Linux management gap",
          "introductionTextBlockOne": "Linux now exceeds 5% of desktop market share. Stack Overflow's 2025 developer survey shows nearly 30% of developers use Linux as their primary work OS.",
          "introductionTextBlockTwo": "Your most important contributors, developers, engineers, and security practitioners, are choosing Linux. And in most organizations, those devices sit outside formal IT management."
        }
      },
