        "url": "/case-study/thumbtack",
        "title": "Thumbtack",
        "lastModifiedAt": 1783044020000,
        "htmlId": "articles--thumbtack--05492ff5a9",
        "sectionRelativeRepoPath": "thumbtack.md",
        "meta": {
          "category": "case study",
          "articleTitle": "Thumbtack migrates more than 90% of Macs with no IT intervention",
          "description": "Thumbtack migrated more than 90% of Macs to Fleet with no IT intervention and now manages devices with GitOps and fast Slack support.",
          "publishedOn": "2026-03-13",
          "authorGitHubUsername": "n/a",
          "authorFullName": "Fleetdm",
          "companyLogoFilename": "thumbtack-logo-197x40@2x.png",
          "quoteAuthorImageFilename": "adam-anklewicz-120x120@2x.png",
          "quoteAuthorName": "Adam Anklewicz",
          "quoteAuthorJobTitle": "Manager, IT Systems Engineering, Thumbtack",
          "quoteContent": "With Fleet, every change gets a second set of eyes on it before it's deployed. That alone has prevented mistakes that would have been very expensive to fix.",
          "companyName": "Thumbtack",
          "companyInfo": "Thumbtack helps homeowners care for and improve their homes by connecting them with local service professionals. Through its platform, people get guidance on what projects to do, when to do them, and who to hire from a community of more than 300,000 service businesses across the United States.",
          "summaryChallenge": "Configuration changes happened in a dashboard. One person clicked, one change went out, no review. Feedback came through a ticket queue. If a configuration was wrong, there was no second set of eyes to catch it before it hit every Mac in the company, and rolling it back was neither fast nor straightforward.",
          "summarySolution": "Thumbtack chose Fleet to bring code review, version control, and rollback to device management. Fleet’s API-first architecture meant configuration changes could be triggered, tested, and deployed inside the same CI/CD workflows engineering already runs.",
          "summaryKeyResults": "Device configuration managed in Git, reviewed before it deploys, and revertable in minutes.; A clear audit history of every configuration change, who made it, and why.; Endpoint changes triggered, tested, and deployed inside the same CI/CD pipelines engineering already runs.; A direct Slack channel to Fleet’s support team, replacing 24-hour ticket cycles.; More than 90% of Macs migrated with no IT-driven enrollment work.;"
        }
      },
