            "required": false,
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "name": "patched_version",
            "description": "The security release that patched this CVE, like \"14.4.1\"",
            "required": false,
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "name": "actively_exploited",
            "description": "\"true\" if this CVE is being actively exploited, \"false\" otherwise",
            "required": false,
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "name": "os_version",
            "description": "If not specified, this is the version of the operating system that the device is running",
            "required": false,
            "type": "text"
          }
        ],
        "url": "https://fleetdm.com/tables/sofa_unpatched_cves",
        "fleetRepoUrl": "https://github.com/fleetdm/fleet/blob/main/schema/tables/sofa_unpatched_cves.yml"
      },
      {
        "name": "software_update",
        "description": "The `software_update` table lists the updates available from Apple's Software Update service on a Mac, one row per available update. When no updates are available, the table returns a single row with `software_update_required` set to `0` and every other column empty.",
        "platforms": [
          "darwin"
        ],
        "examples": "List every available update:\n\n```\nSELECT label, title, version, size_kib, recommended, action FROM software_update WHERE software_update_required = 1;\n```\n\nCheck whether the Mac is fully up to date. This is the check used by Fleet's CIS benchmark policies:\n\n```\nSELECT 1 FROM software_update WHERE software_update_required = 0;\n```\n\nList pending updates while ignoring upgrades to a newer major version of macOS, which Software Update offers alongside regular updates:\n\n```\nSELECT label, title, version\nFROM software_update\nWHERE software_update_required = 1\n  AND NOT (title LIKE 'macOS %' AND CAST(version AS INTEGER) > (SELECT major FROM os_version));\n```",
        "columns": [
          {
            "name": "software_update_required",
            "type": "integer",
            "required": false,
            "description": "`1` if at least one update is available, otherwise `0`. Every row carries the same value."
          },
          {
            "name": "label",
            "type": "text",
            "required": false,
            "description": "Identifier Software Update uses for the update (for example `macOS Tahoe 26.7-25G229`). This is the value `softwareupdate --install` expects. Empty when no updates are available."
          },
          {
            "name": "title",
            "type": "text",
            "required": false,
            "description": "Human-readable name of the update (for example `macOS Tahoe 26.7`)."
          },
          {
            "name": "version",
            "type": "text",
            "required": false,
            "description": "Version of the update (for example `26.7`)."
          },
          {
            "name": "size_kib",
            "type": "integer",
            "required": false,
            "description": "Download size of the update in KiB, as reported by Software Update."
          },
          {
            "name": "recommended",
            "type": "integer",
            "required": false,
            "description": "`1` if Apple marks the update as recommended, otherwise `0`."
          },
          {
            "name": "action",
            "type": "text",
            "required": false,
            "description": "Follow-up action the update requires, such as `restart`. Empty when none is required."
          }
        ],
        "notes": "This table is not a core osquery table. It is included as part of Fleet's agent ([fleetd](https://fleetdm.com/docs/get-started/anatomy#fleetd)).\n\nQuerying this table runs `softwareupdate --list`, which scans Apple's update catalog over the network and typically takes about 10 seconds. fleetd reuses the result of a successful scan for up to 5 minutes, and queries that arrive while a scan is running wait for that scan instead of starting another. If the scan fails (for example, when the Mac is offline) the query returns an error, and if its output can't be interpreted `software_update_required` is reported as `1`, so a compliance check never passes because of a scan that didn't complete.\n\nAvailable updates on a Mac can be displayed in the macOS Graphical User Interface (GUI) by clicking on the Apple menu and then selecting “System Settings”. In the System Settings.app, click General > Software Update.\n\nApple Software Updates can also be listed in Terminal with the following command:\n\n```\nsoftwareupdate --list --verbose\n```\n\n[Update Your Apple Software](https://support.apple.com/guide/personal-safety/update-your-apple-software-ips4930e3486/web)",
        "evented": false,
        "url": "https://fleetdm.com/tables/software_update",
        "fleetRepoUrl": "https://github.com/fleetdm/fleet/blob/main/schema/tables/software_update.yml"
      },
      {
        "name": "ssh_configs",
        "description": "A table of parsed ssh_configs.",
